Comparison and Optimization of Techniques About Constructing the Anchor
Cable Groups by Piercing the Shield into the Adjacent Foundation Pits
HU Jun
( China Railway 14th Bureau Group Tunnel Engineering Co. Ltd., Jinan Shandong 250013, China)
Abstract: It is unavoidable that various buildings and underground obstacles have to be pierced due to the application of the
shield. Usually, the foundation pits′supporting structure applies cable bolting where tall buildings have been finished on the
both sides of the road. And the length of that cable bolting is closely related to the depth of the pits and the hydrogeology
conditions. Many challenges arise from the cable bolting that is usually left in the ground after completing the foundation pits.
And the solutions to these challenges mainly depend on actual hydrogeology conditions, the cable bolting design and
construction situations, and the surrounding engineering environment. On the basis of the shield tunneling construction in a
watery and weak stratum, this paper puts forward several different ways to deal with the cable bolting, and compares them from
the aspects of construction effect, construction risk, construction period, and economy. With shield′s targeted and effective
design for the construction plan and anchor area′s proper opening conditions under normal pressure in place, the anchor area
can be directly pierced by the shield, minimizing its environmental impacts and decreasing the cost.
Key words: shield construction; watery and weak stratum; anchor cable group; scheme comparison and optimization
